From 78b3dc0ebe845b1b27bf8f5431a7471c5918816e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:07:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] website: typecheck generates Next's route types first
 (clean checkouts and CI failed)

`tsc --noEmit` on a fresh checkout fails with 4 errors (PageProps and RouteContext not found): those global
types live in .next/types and next-env.d.ts, which only `next build`/`next dev` create and git ignores. The
CI "check" job runs typecheck straight after `npm ci`, so it could never pass. `next typegen` (0.4 s) writes
them without a build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N9g7Xn7RWKaJF173G8V173
---
 website/web/package.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/website/web/package.json b/website/web/package.json
index 70fa123..4b7dd22 100644
--- a/website/web/package.json
+++ b/website/web/package.json
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
     "dev": "next dev -p 3000",
     "build": "next build",
     "start": "next start",
-    "typecheck": "tsc --noEmit",
+    "typecheck": "next typegen && tsc --noEmit",
     "lint": "eslint .",
     "format": "prettier --write .",
     "format:check": "prettier --check .",
